  _push(`<p>Properties:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.a</code>, <code>.b</code>, <code>.c</code>, <code>.d</code>, <code>.e</code>, <code>.f</code></td><td>Six numeric SVG matrix coefficients</td></tr><tr><td><code>.tx</code></td><td>Getter alias of <code>.e</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.ty</code></td><td>Getter alias of <code>.f</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Methods:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.multiply(other)</code></td><td>Matrix product <code>this * other</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.then(other)</code></td><td>Application-order composition <code>other.multiply(this)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.applyToPoint(pointLike)</code></td><td>Transforms a Point, including translation</td></tr><tr><td><code>.applyToVector(vectorLike)</code></td><td>Transforms a Vector, excluding translation</td></tr><tr><td><code>.determinant()</code></td><td><code>a*d - b*c</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.inverse(epsilon = EPSILON)</code></td><td>Inverse Matrix, or <code>null</code> when determinant is within epsilon</td></tr><tr><td><code>.isIdentity(epsilon = EPSILON)</code></td><td>Approximate identity check</td></tr><tr><td><code>.equals(other, epsilon = EPSILON)</code></td><td>Absolute tolerance across six coefficients</td></tr><tr><td><code>.nearlyEquals(other, epsilon = EPSILON)</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.equals()</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.toArray()</code></td><td><code>[a, b, c, d, e, f]</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.toSvgString()</code></td><td>Space-separated six-value string</td></tr><tr><td><code>.toSVG()</code></td><td><code>matrix(a b c d e f)</code> string</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Different from the Studio Matrix</p><p>This advanced <code>.inverse()</code> returns <code>null</code> for a singular matrix. The root DSL&#39;s smaller <code>Matrix</code> class throws an Error instead.</p></div><p>Static constructors and aliases:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Constructor</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Matrix.identity()</code></td><td>Identity matrix</td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.translation(x, y = 0)</code></td><td>Translation matrix</td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.translation(pointLike)</code></td><td>Translation using <code>.x</code> and <code>.y</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.translate(...)</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.translation(...)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.scaling(x, y = x)</code></td><td>Scale matrix</td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.scale(...)</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.scaling(...)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.rotation(radians)</code></td><td>Rotation matrix</td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.rotate(radians)</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.rotation()</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.skewX(radians)</code></td><td>Horizontal skew</td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.skewY(radians)</code></td><td>Vertical skew</td></tr><tr><td><code>Matrix.skew(xRadians = 0, yRadians = 0)</code></td><td>Combined skew</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="bounds" tabindex="-1">Bounds <a class="header-anchor" href="#bounds" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Bounds&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="new-bounds-minx-infinity-miny-infinity-maxx-infinity-maxy-infinity" tabindex="-1"><code>new Bounds(minX = Infinity, minY = Infinity, maxX = -Infinity, maxY = -Infinity)</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#new-bounds-minx-infinity-miny-infinity-maxx-infinity-maxy-infinity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;\`new Bounds(minX = Infinity, minY = Infinity, maxX = -Infinity, maxY = -Infinity)\`&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Stores an immutable axis-aligned bounding box. <code>new Bounds()</code> is empty.</p>`);
